=== meta
title   = "Coding workflow tool dictionary"
===

%% The coding workflow's starting dictionary (spec §5.3): the read-only tools
%% are allowed in every state; editing is the use `edit`, which only #implement
%% declares; the common test commands are the use `test`, which only #verify
%% declares. Any other tool runs as usual; write a row here to deny one or bind
%% it to a use.

=== table {#tools}
| tool             | for  | allow | deny | default | params |
|------------------|------|-------|------|---------|--------|
| Read             |      | *     |      |         |        |
| Grep             |      | *     |      |         |        |
| Glob             |      | *     |      |         |        |
| Edit             | edit |       |      | yes     |        |
| Write            | edit |       |      |         |        |
| NotebookEdit     | edit |       |      |         |        |
| apply_patch      | edit |       |      |         |        |
| Bash(npm test)   | test |       |      | yes     |        |
| Bash(pnpm test)  | test |       |      |         |        |
| Bash(yarn test)  | test |       |      |         |        |
| Bash(cargo test) | test |       |      |         |        |
| Bash(pytest)     | test |       |      |         |        |
| Bash(go test)    | test |       |      |         |        |
===
